  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Certum id est de jure civi-</l>
    <l n="2">li,quod per Imperatores Chri-</l>
    <l n="3">stianos correctum (antea enim</l>
    <l n="4">consuetudine obtinebant) ad</l>
    <l n="5">humanitatem &amp; æquitatem</l>
    <l n="6">redactum fuit. Et quia duella</l>
    <l n="7">talia, nihil aliud sunt, quam</l>
    <l n="8">gladiatorum, vel lanistarum</l>
    <l n="9">commissiones , quæ penitus</l>
    <l n="10">sunt sublatæ. Ita enim Con-</l>
    <l n="11">stantinus Imperator. <i>Cruenta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>spectacula in otio civili &amp; domesti-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>cā quiete non placent : quapropter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>omnino gladiatores esse prohibemus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">Et quia exploratio virium at-</l>
    <l n="16">que fortitudinis esse debet ci-</l>
    <l n="17">tra injustitiam. Ea quippe so-</l>
    <l n="18">lum fortitudo, quæ virtuti</l>
    <l n="19">juncta est, eaque solummodo</l>
    <l n="20">laudabilis. Et quia de jure sub-</l>
    <l n="21">lata ea genera spectaculorum,</l>
    <l n="22">in quibus ursi,pantheri,leones</l>
    <l n="23">cum hominibus committe-</l>
    <l n="24">bantur ; multo magis, in qui-</l>
    <l n="25">bus homines cum hominibus</l>
    <l n="26">ad vulnera &amp; cædem[?] crudelem</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="Cruenta spectacula in" line_from="11" line_to="11">l.unic. Cod. de Gladiat. tollend. Novell. 69.§.1.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Printing as read: "spectacula" and "Cruenta" are italic; the margin reference is printed in small type, one note. "juncta" has a diacritic over the c that is unclear; read as juncta. "cædem" is partly unclear in the scan ([?]). The text ends mid-sentence at "crudelem"; the catchword "com-" stands alone at the right below the last line. Printed signature "F 3" at the foot.</notes>
